\pxi-2.6,l2.6;1. STIRRUP SPACING IS DIMENSIONED TO BAR CENTERLINES.\P2. REINFORCEMENT IS SHOWN REPRESENTATIVELY: THE FIRST AND LAST BAR OF EACH RUN ARE DRAWN.\P3. FOR SECTIONS A-A, B-B AND C-C, SEE SHEET B4-2. FOR VIEWS D-D AND E-E AND PEDESTAL DETAI
  3
LS, SEE SHEET B4-3.\P4. THE SOIL REINFORCEMENT ATTACHED TO THE BACKWALL SHALL BE DESIGNED BY A SPECIALTY ENGINEER FOR A SERVICE LOAD OF ___ K/FT AND A FACTORED LOAD OF ___ K/FT USING THE DESIGN CRITERIA FOR PERMANENT MSE WALLS. COST OF FURNISHING AND
  3
 INSTALLING THE SOIL REINFORCEMENT IS CONSIDERED INCIDENTAL TO THE COST OF THE END BENT.\P5. FOR REINFORCING BAR LIST, SEE SHEET B4-9.\P6. PILE OFFSETS ARE FROM THE PGL, + TO THE RIGHT LOOKING UP-STATION. CUTOFF ELEVATIONS ARE TO THE NEAREST 0.1 FT.\
  1
P7. MODEL CHECK (REMOVE BEFORE ISSUE): BACKWALL TOP AT CAP END END BENT 1 IS 47.192 IN THE CAD MODEL AND 47.132 IN THE SELECTED GEOMETRY CAD TABLES; RECONCILE BEFORE ISSUE.
